# engine/schema is the input validator (ADR-0042). Small, pure, and the code
# whose failure mode is "a check the caller was told ran, did not" — plus it
# carries the conformance suite, so a drop here means the specification's own
# cases stopped being exercised.
github.com/aaron-au/shift/engine/schema 88
github.com/aaron-au/shift/engine/spill 96
github.com/aaron-au/shift/engine/stream 84
# hub/internal/api 88 -> 87 (2026-08-06, ADR-0049 gateway pairing).
#
# The gateway realm added ~130 statements of handler code. Its behaviour is
# covered — validation, the token being served exactly once and never again,
# the full pairing exchange against a real gateway, a wrong token, a spent
# token, rotation, deletion-as-revocation, malformed ids, and a runner
# credential being refused the realm entirely.
#
# What is NOT covered is the remaining error arms of adoptGateway and
# listGateways: store failures mid-adoption (LearnGatewayFingerprint racing
# MarkGatewayAdopted) that need failure injection to reach. Writing tests that
# contrive those paths would move the number without asserting anything a user
# would notice, which is the opposite of why the gate exists.
#
# Recorded here rather than done quietly. If failure injection lands in the
# store test harness, this goes back to 88.
github.com/aaron-au/shift/hub/internal/api 87
