# httpsec is the SSRF/network guard shared by every outbound connector. It was
# only ever held by the permissive `default`; it is small, pure, and the code
# whose failure mode is "a connector reached somewhere it must not", so it gets
# an explicit floor at what it already achieves.
github.com/aaron-au/shift/pkg/httpsec 98

# The control-plane CA (ADR-0044). What is uncovered is the signing-failure and
# serial-generation arms, which need a broken crypto source; every rule that
# decides WHAT gets issued — subject, usages, key strength, proof of possession
# — is covered.
github.com/aaron-au/shift/hub/internal/gwpush 81
github.com/aaron-au/shift/hub/internal/gwsync 81
github.com/aaron-au/shift/hub/internal/pki 88

# The logging setup and vocabulary (ADR-0046). What is uncovered is Fatalf
